# 📡 Wireless Standards in Networking

Today I learned about wireless standards used in computer networking. These standards define how devices communicate wirelessly over short and long distances.

---

## 1️⃣ Wi-Fi Standards (IEEE 802.11)

Wi-Fi is used for Wireless Local Area Networks (WLAN).

| Standard | Frequency Band | Maximum Speed | Key Feature |
|-----------|----------------|---------------|--------------|
| 802.11a | 5 GHz | 54 Mbps | Less interference |
| 802.11b | 2.4 GHz | 11 Mbps | Longer range |
| 802.11g | 2.4 GHz | 54 Mbps | Faster than 802.11b |
| 802.11n | 2.4 / 5 GHz | Up to 600 Mbps | Uses MIMO technology |
| 802.11ac (Wi-Fi 5) | 5 GHz | ~1 Gbps | High-speed performance |
| 802.11ax (Wi-Fi 6) | 2.4 / 5 GHz | Multi-Gbps | Better efficiency & device handling |

👉 Used in homes, offices, campuses for internet access.

---

## 2️⃣ Bluetooth (IEEE 802.15.1)

- Short-range wireless communication  
- Low power consumption  
- Used for Personal Area Networks (PAN)  
- Common in headphones, keyboards, smart devices  
- Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) is used in IoT devices  

👉 Best for connecting personal devices.

---

## 3️⃣ Zigbee (IEEE 802.15.4)

- Very low power usage  
- Supports mesh networking  
- Designed for automation and IoT  
- Used in smart homes and sensor networks  

👉 Ideal for low-data smart devices.

---

## 4️⃣ Cellular Standards

| Generation | Main Focus |
|------------|------------|
| 2G | Voice communication |
| 3G | Internet access |
| 4G LTE | High-speed mobile data |
| 5G | Ultra-fast speed & low latency |

👉 Used in Wide Area Networks (WAN) for mobile connectivity.

---

# 🔎 Key Comparison

| Standard | Range | Speed | Power Consumption | Use Case |
|----------|--------|--------|------------------|------------|
| Wi-Fi | Medium | High | Medium | Internet access |
| Bluetooth | Short | Low | Very Low | Personal devices |
| Zigbee | Short-Medium | Very Low | Extremely Low | Smart automation |
| Cellular | Very Large | Very High | High | Mobile broadband |

---

## ✅ Key Takeaways

- Wi-Fi is used for high-speed local networking.
- Bluetooth is used for short-range personal communication.
- Zigbee is designed for IoT and automation.
- Cellular networks provide long-distance mobile connectivity.
